# Allowlist: the build context is the repo root, which on a developer machine or the EC2 host
# also holds .env, .dev-credentials.txt, dumps and real student spreadsheets. Sending only what
# the images are built from keeps those out of the build entirely, not just out of the final layer.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!Caddyfile
!apps/
!packages/
!templates/import-template.xlsx

# Never sent, even from inside the allowed directories. Installs and builds happen inside the
# image, so local node_modules/dist would only make the result depend on the machine.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env*
**/.dev-credentials.txt
**/*.dump
**/*.xlsx
!templates/import-template.xlsx
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/.DS_Store
apps/api/test
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
